WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.115
Arena helps when two plausible designs could
take the code in different directions.

2
00:00:06.115 --> 00:00:08.800
This run uses two scripted model seats.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.142
Each seat builds its own greeting
candidate in a separate worktree.

4
00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:17.382
The scorecard favors the
simpler parser as a base.

5
00:00:17.382 --> 00:00:21.400
The other candidate contributes
normalization for blank names.

6
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:40.039
The parent combines those two parts
and runs both checks on the result.

7
00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.427
You can see exactly what made
it into the final change.
